-- ex39 Tier 3 opaque: matrix view is native algebra, graph and behaviour-tree views are select-and-dispatch. Twin of 39-tier3-opaque.bqn.
-- Adj is registered as a set-valued fiber-matrix: fiber i holds row i's BITS, so the matrix view's row fold +/ Adj@row is the out-degree 2 1 3 0 2 (node 3's all-zero row folds to the identity 0).
-- shortestPath and runBehaviorTree are identity-envelope verbs: the host receives the selection and the whole payload, ano writes nothing. expect btree pins the payloads bit-identical after dispatch; expect outDeg doubling as the stmt-2 no-write witness.
-- Left to the .bqn twin: env ≡ 1 3 4 and /cursor ≡ ⟨3⟩ (the envelopes are exactly the hostile/cursor fixtures, definitional), adj bit-identity (a set-valued column has no expect form), and the "patrol" payload gather (BQN-internal).
--! registry 39-tier3-opaque
--! expect outDeg = 2 1 3 0 2
--! expect btree = seek flee guard patrol idle

Node , OutDeg = +/ Adj@row
Hostile , shortestPath via Adj
@cursor , runBehaviorTree
